(2870692, 400106, 35804, '<td valign="top">...that is the BEST umbrella I have seen in a looooong time...great shot.</td>', '...that is the BEST umbrella I have seen in a looooong time...great shot.', '2006-09-27 22:11:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870702, 400079, 6999, '<td valign="top">As with some other shots of this kind, I wonder if you might not have benefitted from greater depth of field; the road and landscape are perhaps too far out of focus for comfort. I like the idea, but the streaks of the wiper blades don''t seem to add much.</td>', 'As with some other shots of this kind, I wonder if you might not have benefitted from greater depth of field; the road and landscape are perhaps too far out of focus for comfort. I like the idea, but the streaks of the wiper blades don''t seem to add much.', '2006-09-27 22:14:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870709, 400121, 35804, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot! I love the square format, works perfectly for the image...textures, reflection, composition, and motion, this has it all...very nice work.</td>', 'Excellent shot! I love the square format, works perfectly for the image...textures, reflection, composition, and motion, this has it all...very nice work.', '2006-09-27 22:15:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870718, 400613, 35804, '<td valign="top">Beautiful color and focus...simple and lovely.</td>', 'Beautiful color and focus...simple and lovely.', '2006-09-27 22:17:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870719, 401309, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good colour and focus, though the grass seeds maybe intrude a touch too much in front of that particular blade for neatness. You might have found a stronger compositional line if you''d been able to place it more definitely on a diagonal - especially as there isn''t another parallel element to help prioritise your primary subject. Though I guess focus and the water drops go a long way to achieving that.</td>', 'Good colour and focus, though the grass seeds maybe intrude a touch too much in front of that particular blade for neatness. You might have found a stronger compositional line if you''d been able to place it more definitely on a diagonal - especially as there isn''t another parallel element to help prioritise your primary subject. Though I guess focus and the water drops go a long way to achieving that.', '2006-09-27 22:17:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870723, 400146, 6999, '<td valign="top">Quite a nice approach. maybe more contrast might have brought out the geometry more strongly, though of course it would require care to keep the grey day feel that you have. Reasonable composition, but the top rioght corner disturbs things a touch.</td>', 'Quite a nice approach. maybe more contrast might have brought out the geometry more strongly, though of course it would require care to keep the grey day feel that you have. Reasonable composition, but the top rioght corner disturbs things a touch.', '2006-09-27 22:19:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870757, 401758, 6999, '<td valign="top">A quite pleasing old school image - with some impact, although perhaps the DOF could have been even more extreme for real effect.</td>', 'A quite pleasing old school image - with some impact, although perhaps the DOF could have been even more extreme for real effect.', '2006-09-27 22:29:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870763, 402218, 6999, '<td valign="top">A strong composition, and catches some of that feel of approaching rain after a long dry time. The structure that the post and wire lends to the scene is essential.</td>', 'A strong composition, and catches some of that feel of approaching rain after a long dry time. The structure that the post and wire lends to the scene is essential.', '2006-09-27 22:31:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870776, 402040, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good tones, good detail, and exposure is spot on. I don''t find any sense of compositional structure in it, though: nothing to balance that corner of grass, but the reflected light in the negative space areas helps with the impression of an overcast day: but you have that already in the cap-stones on the wall. Better than most so far, though.</td>', 'Good tones, good detail, and exposure is spot on. I don''t find any sense of compositional structure in it, though: nothing to balance that corner of grass, but the reflected light in the negative space areas helps with the impression of an overcast day: but you have that already in the cap-stones on the wall. Better than most so far, though.', '2006-09-27 22:35:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870781, 400807, 6999, '<td valign="top">Nice shooting. I like the dynamic, and for once someone has used the out of focus distortions of rain on window rather than simply focussing on the drops. it lends a mystery and sadness top the lines of those bricks and trees.</td>', 'Nice shooting. I like the dynamic, and for once someone has used the out of focus distortions of rain on window rather than simply focussing on the drops. it lends a mystery and sadness top the lines of those bricks and trees.', '2006-09-27 22:37:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870787, 400121, 6999, '<td valign="top">Nice work - especially the lead going out of frame, given a parallel dynamic by the line of the path.</td>', 'Nice work - especially the lead going out of frame, given a parallel dynamic by the line of the path.', '2006-09-27 22:38:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870793, 400240, 6999, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, i think - compositionally, though I''m not sure you''ve quite pulled it off - perhaps the flower''s structure just isn''t regular enough for the image to handle this partial treatment; that trick usually seems to depend on the viewer having the impression that the object is so regular there is simply no point in including the rest of it. I think also there''s something amiss with the intensity of these colours - over saturation, or simply over-exposure (I''m sure you could have exposed a stop less and had more impact)? The pink certainly becomes kind of messy and indistinct toward the centre of the flower.</td>', 'I like the idea, i think - compositionally, though I''m not sure you''ve quite pulled it off - perhaps the flower''s structure just isn''t regular enough for the image to handle this partial treatment; that trick usually seems to depend on the viewer having the impression that the object is so regular there is simply no point in including the rest of it. I think also there''s something amiss with the intensity of these colours - over saturation, or simply over-exposure (I''m sure you could have exposed a stop less and had more impact)? The pink certainly becomes kind of messy and indistinct toward the centre of the flower.', '2006-09-27 22:41:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870798, 398674, 6999, '<td valign="top">I like the prgressive contrast against the bar of light - the sudden reversal; perhaps you might have made more of that? It seems so relegated in this composition. Good detail though, and sense of fragility.</td>', 'I like the prgressive contrast against the bar of light - the sudden reversal; perhaps you might have made more of that? It seems so relegated in this composition. Good detail though, and sense of fragility.', '2006-09-27 22:42:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870800, 399446, 6999, '<td valign="top">Lihgt very neatly handled - good exposure, and good processing.</td>', 'Lihgt very neatly handled - good exposure, and good processing.', '2006-09-27 22:43:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2870809, 399156, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice shot but I wonder how it would look with a little less saturation.</td>', 'Nice shot but I wonder how it would look with a little less saturation.', '2006-09-27 22:47:06.000000', NULL, 1),
