(2895343, 402161, 39057, '<td valign="top">Well you can see that I was the 4th person to comment on your shot and gave it a 10. Good job.<br/> <br/>Also, how many extention tubes did you use? What was the total length of the tubes? Please PM me with info!<br/> <br/>Kenskid<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i> 10    Please PM me with your cam/lens/extension tube etc set-up asap. I can''t wait til the challenge is over. I need that info NOW! I''m not kidding ! </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-10-04 10:02:56.</i></td>', 'Well you can see that I was the 4th person to comment on your shot and gave it a 10. Good job. Also, how many extention tubes did you use? What was the total length of the tubes? Please PM me with info! Kenskid Originally posted by kenskid: 10    Please PM me with your cam/lens/extension tube etc set-up asap. I can''t wait til the challenge is over. I need that info NOW! I''m not kidding ! ', '2006-10-04 11:01:54.000000', '2006-10-04 11:02:56.000000', 0),
(2895348, 400673, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I''d really like to see this image shot at a different time of day.  I see a hint of terrific color on the back of this chair, but that portion of the image is a bit underexposed, even with the fill flash.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> In a word: harsh.  Your time of day created some hard and contrasting areas that battle for the eye''s attention.  Unfortunately, the subject isn''t strong enough to hold the eye.  My eye is pulled directly to the lower, left-hand corner, and there is nothing else in the frame to pull it away from there.  The shadow created from the fill flash also created some awkward shadows of the chair and the foot.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> The main problem with the content is that there is no rain in an image entered into the rain challenge.  The composition isn''t bad, but I''d like to see it loosened up just a bit.  Cropping this tight gives a cramped, boxed-in feeling instead of the relaxing feeling that the subject matter warrants.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Considering the challenge subject and the harsh lighting of the image, I think that this one scored near where it should have.  Even leaving the subject as-is and making the needed lighting changes would have bumped this one up considerably in score.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: I''d really like to see this image shot at a different time of day.  I see a hint of terrific color on the back of this chair, but that portion of the image is a bit underexposed, even with the fill flash. Lighting: In a word: harsh.  Your time of day created some hard and contrasting areas that battle for the eye''s attention.  Unfortunately, the subject isn''t strong enough to hold the eye.  My eye is pulled directly to the lower, left-hand corner, and there is nothing else in the frame to pull it away from there.  The shadow created from the fill flash also created some awkward shadows of the chair and the foot. Composition/Content: The main problem with the content is that there is no rain in an image entered into the rain challenge.  The composition isn''t bad, but I''d like to see it loosened up just a bit.  Cropping this tight gives a cramped, boxed-in feeling instead of the relaxing feeling that the subject matter warrants. My Opinion: Considering the challenge subject and the harsh lighting of the image, I think that this one scored near where it should have.  Even leaving the subject as-is and making the needed lighting changes would have bumped this one up considerably in score. Eric', '2006-10-04 11:02:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895409, 402252, 24454, '<td valign="top">Genius!   What an incredible gallery of these amazing shots you have!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Genius!   What an incredible gallery of these amazing shots you have! ', '2006-10-04 11:19:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895416, 401728, 24454, '<td valign="top">She is so beautiful, and looks to be enjoying herself so much!  Amazing photo!  Amazing!</td>', 'She is so beautiful, and looks to be enjoying herself so much!  Amazing photo!  Amazing!', '2006-10-04 11:20:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895421, 401644, 48890, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i>So what was the answer with the blurred central bike? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The shot was shot at f/1.4, so DOF should have been pretty slim, which explains the unsharp bike in the middle.  I think that the biker *appears* to be sharper than he is because the backlighting creates a contrasty halo around him, sort of a natural oversharpen effect.  So, I think that the effect of uneven sharpness distribution is just a visual mistake.</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo:So what was the answer with the blurred central bike?  The shot was shot at f/1.4, so DOF should have been pretty slim, which explains the unsharp bike in the middle.  I think that the biker *appears* to be sharper than he is because the backlighting creates a contrasty halo around him, sort of a natural oversharpen effect.  So, I think that the effect of uneven sharpness distribution is just a visual mistake.', '2006-10-04 11:21:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895429, 399867, 24454, '<td valign="top">How beautiful!!!   I agree with jdannels that it is very underrated.  I guess if the voters didn''t see raindrops in the sky they counted off :(<br/></td>', 'How beautiful!!!   I agree with jdannels that it is very underrated.  I guess if the voters didn''t see raindrops in the sky they counted off :(', '2006-10-04 11:23:05.000000', NULL, 0),
