(2895441, 399156, 24454, '<td valign="top">I thought I was the only one who headed out to the zoo for every challenge :)   You can''t even tell you''re at the zoo tho, and this is really awesome!   Perfect for this challenge!<br/> <br/></td>', 'I thought I was the only one who headed out to the zoo for every challenge :)   You can''t even tell you''re at the zoo tho, and this is really awesome!   Perfect for this challenge! ', '2006-10-04 11:27:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895465, 401644, 48890, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i>I gave you a 6, which is one of the lowest scores I''ve given you. ... It just didn''t grab me while I was voting. uh-oh... maybe I''m becoming a focus nazi! :O </i></td></tr></table> <br/>:)  Well, this picture has very little symbolism, which is, I guess, why you liked it less than my other pictures.  This is, also, why it scored so high.  Look at the top winners of any challenge: most of them lack any kind of semantics.<br/> <br/>Personally, I think that the only thing that "makes" this shot is its cinema-like appearance: it has this "drive", which is, probably, a combination of high contrast, lighting, and dynamics.  I definitely don''t think that this is my best picture.  But I needed a score above 5.6; in fact I need to score above 5.6 three more times to get that man with the bottle off my personal page. :)  And I am back to my usual sub-5 score with my Free Study XIII entry.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous:I gave you a 6, which is one of the lowest scores I''ve given you. ... It just didn''t grab me while I was voting. uh-oh... maybe I''m becoming a focus nazi! :O  :)  Well, this picture has very little symbolism, which is, I guess, why you liked it less than my other pictures.  This is, also, why it scored so high.  Look at the top winners of any challenge: most of them lack any kind of semantics. Personally, I think that the only thing that "makes" this shot is its cinema-like appearance: it has this "drive", which is, probably, a combination of high contrast, lighting, and dynamics.  I definitely don''t think that this is my best picture.  But I needed a score above 5.6; in fact I need to score above 5.6 three more times to get that man with the bottle off my personal page. :)  And I am back to my usual sub-5 score with my Free Study XIII entry.', '2006-10-04 11:31:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895515, 402231, 48890, '<td valign="top">Hey, Don, and I gave *your* picture a 6, and it''s your third best score and and a top 20 finish. :)  So, we are quits, I guess.  More than that, I was wrong thinking that this <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=402144" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/561/thumb/402144.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/561/thumb/402144.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/561/thumb/402144.jpg"/></a> was your entry.<br/> <br/>The sky is quite drammatic here, but this is the only thing that I like about this shot.  Perhaps I am missing something.  I think that the raising diagonal contradicts the "before the storm" atmosphere, and do not understand the purpose of that contradiction (was it intended?).  The horses are but tiny specs in the image, and are stuck together.<br/> <br/>I explained what I liked about my own entry into this challenge in response to your comment.  It would be interesting to hear your thoughs about this image.</td>', 'Hey, Don, and I gave *your* picture a 6, and it''s your third best score and and a top 20 finish. :)  So, we are quits, I guess.  More than that, I was wrong thinking that this  was your entry. The sky is quite drammatic here, but this is the only thing that I like about this shot.  Perhaps I am missing something.  I think that the raising diagonal contradicts the "before the storm" atmosphere, and do not understand the purpose of that contradiction (was it intended?).  The horses are but tiny specs in the image, and are stuck together. I explained what I liked about my own entry into this challenge in response to your comment.  It would be interesting to hear your thoughs about this image.', '2006-10-04 11:42:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895568, 401728, 52713, '<td valign="top">Not your usual style but a familiar result. Good job on branching out and still maintianing your high standards.</td>', 'Not your usual style but a familiar result. Good job on branching out and still maintianing your high standards.', '2006-10-04 12:03:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895592, 400121, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful shot, Lori!  Beautiful composition - and you did a great job capturing the rain drops.  But it''s dear Winston who carries the show here.  Very nice work!</td>', 'This is a wonderful shot, Lori!  Beautiful composition - and you did a great job capturing the rain drops.  But it''s dear Winston who carries the show here.  Very nice work!', '2006-10-04 12:11:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895630, 400121, 38127, '<td valign="top">Nothing stopping you from cloning it out now :) ... <br/> <br/>I absolutely love this shot... would love it even more without the leash, it''ll give it a more lonely, down and out feeling.  Brilliant. <br/> <br/>Have you looked at any of E301 pictures or xion? I think this might be equally brilliant if edited something like they do with the stark b&amp;w''s <br/>Having said that however, I do love what you''ve already done and the mood you have created with your editing ;)</td>', 'Nothing stopping you from cloning it out now :) ...  I absolutely love this shot... would love it even more without the leash, it''ll give it a more lonely, down and out feeling.  Brilliant.  Have you looked at any of E301 pictures or xion? I think this might be equally brilliant if edited something like they do with the stark b&w''s Having said that however, I do love what you''ve already done and the mood you have created with your editing ;)', '2006-10-04 12:21:46.000000', NULL, 0),
