(2896231, 402252, 43410, '<td valign="top">i''m speachless.  just when i think your shots can''t get any more creative, you outdo yourself.  just another reason as to why you''re one of my, and 238904723947 other people''s, favorite photographer.<br/> <br/>great job as always :)</td>', 'i''m speachless.  just when i think your shots can''t get any more creative, you outdo yourself.  just another reason as to why you''re one of my, and 238904723947 other people''s, favorite photographer. great job as always :)', '2006-10-04 15:24:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896459, 401873, 52352, '<td valign="top">I absolutely love this.</td>', 'I absolutely love this.', '2006-10-04 16:36:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896528, 402161, 39057, '<td valign="top">IMO this is not a centered comp. My eyes are drawn comfortably to the grasshoppers eye. From there my eye is drawn up the OOF flower petal and then down the infocus flower to the "cheek"...then back to the eye.<br/> <br/>It is a fluid shot which makes you want to keep looking.<br/> <br/>Kenskid</td>', 'IMO this is not a centered comp. My eyes are drawn comfortably to the grasshoppers eye. From there my eye is drawn up the OOF flower petal and then down the infocus flower to the "cheek"...then back to the eye. It is a fluid shot which makes you want to keep looking. Kenskid', '2006-10-04 16:57:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896586, 402231, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by agenkin:</b></div><hr/><i>I explained what I liked about my own entry into this challenge in response to your comment.  It would be interesting to hear your thoughs about this image. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>First of all, my taste is far more developed than my abilities! :) The picture you thought was mine is indeed my taste. This picture was taken out the window of a semi-moving car, and I was amazed at the quality of the light. Not the composition, not the symbolism, just the light. So I cropped it and created a little <i>frisson</i> with the title, to make it more interesting. And there you have it. Certainly not my third favorite picture! But I''m glad to please people every now and then! :)<br/> <br/>Notice we gave each other 6s, and our scores were just a little higher than that. I''ve heard it said the secret to a high score is to offend the least amount of people. I will post the original and I will *also* post outtakes that I think are more typical of my taste, and would have scored a full point lower, at least.</td>', 'Originally posted by agenkin:I explained what I liked about my own entry into this challenge in response to your comment.  It would be interesting to hear your thoughs about this image.   First of all, my taste is far more developed than my abilities! :) The picture you thought was mine is indeed my taste. This picture was taken out the window of a semi-moving car, and I was amazed at the quality of the light. Not the composition, not the symbolism, just the light. So I cropped it and created a little frisson with the title, to make it more interesting. And there you have it. Certainly not my third favorite picture! But I''m glad to please people every now and then! :) Notice we gave each other 6s, and our scores were just a little higher than that. I''ve heard it said the secret to a high score is to offend the least amount of people. I will post the original and I will *also* post outtakes that I think are more typical of my taste, and would have scored a full point lower, at least.', '2006-10-04 17:25:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896638, 401738, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''d say you picked the right one - this has a lovely feel to it.  Nice tones, really depicts a rainy day quite nicely!</td>', 'I''d say you picked the right one - this has a lovely feel to it.  Nice tones, really depicts a rainy day quite nicely!', '2006-10-04 17:43:26.000000', NULL, 0),
